cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Public element sets against reconstructed orbits through the storms of 2024:
  what was measured, what was corrected, and what it does not show
message: >-
  Cite this frozen paper and supporting-code release when using its measurements.
  The paper states the measured population, independent checks and limitations.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Bhana
    given-names: Nikhil
    email: "nikhilb9244@gmail.com"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-2220-627X"
    city: "Cape Town"
    country: "ZA"
repository-code: "https://github.com/nikhilb9244-cloud/driftwatch"
url: "https://github.com/nikhilb9244-cloud/driftwatch/releases/tag/paper-2026-09-v1"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22656992"
abstract: >-
  Public SGP4 element sets are compared with reconstructed orbits for fifteen
  spacecraft at 460 to 1,338 km over a quiet window and three storm windows,
  with 1,201 usable sets and laser ranging as a further reference. The paper
  reports prediction horizons, covariance calibration, observed-ap storm-term
  skill, the held-out dSGP4 evaluation, post-burn fit errors, radio horizons,
  and convention and provenance faults exposed by independent checks. These
  are measurements on the stated population, not operational guarantees.
keywords:
  - conjunction assessment
  - space situational awareness
  - SGP4
  - geomagnetic storm
  - thermospheric drag
  - orbit uncertainty
license: MIT
version: paper-2026-09-v1
date-released: "2026-09-08"
